        <para>On the immutable &productnameshort; the root file system is mounted to ensure stability and reliablity. Modifications to the file system are handled by the &tr-up; command. To ease the work of administrators that are used to work with standard &productnameshort;, a wrapper that enables the user to call <command>zypper</command> directly, has been introduced. This article provides an overview how <command>zypper</command> interacts with an immutable system, from builtin read-only commands to seamless system modifications using the wrapper.</para>
